<div id="2026-09-27-ai-model-policy" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-27 — AI model usage policy tables (Result classes only)</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Added three Result classes for a per-model usage policy: <code>AiModelPolicy</code> (identity + status + notes + judge attribution), <code>AiModelPolicyRule</code> (one row per criterion), <code>AiModelPolicyHistory</code> (append-only audit). Registered in <code>Model::Schema::Ency</code>. Also extended <code>Model::AI2::UsageMonitor</code> with <code>agent_effectiveness</code> — per agent × model success rate, grounded rate, flagged (uncited) sentences per call, cost per successful call and cost wasted on failed calls — surfaced on <code>/ai/usage</code> as a cost-effectiveness card, and fixed the ledger window that was pinned to 14 days in <code>Controller::AI</code> and <code>Controller::AI::Usage</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Cost tracking existed but nothing measured value for money or recorded how a model should be used in future. Criteria are stored as <em>rows</em> rather than columns so a new criterion ("only for site CSC", "max $0.02 per 1k tokens") needs no migration. Tables are not created yet — that is a schema-branch job via schema-compare, never hand-written DDL.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/AiModelPolicy.pm</code>, <code>AiModelPolicyRule.pm</code>, <code>AiModelPolicyHistory.pm</code>, <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency.pm</code>, <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/UsageMonitor.pm</code>, <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/AI.pm</code>, <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/AI/Usage.pm</code>, <code>Comserv/root/ai/usage.tt</code>, <code>Comserv/root/ai/usage_effectiveness_card.tt</code>, <code>Comserv/root/static/js/ai/usage-monitor.js</code></p>
</div>